Excerpts from netnews.rec.games.hack: 29-Apr-93 Re: Some thoughts and
comme.. by Danh T. Vo@cs.washington 
> I am sick and tired of people suggesting making the game more difficult, 
> especially that idea of having monster zap wands of cancellation at you.  
> Do you seriously find it fun to have all your armors, weapons <including 
> that wonderful Mjollnir) and everything else demagicked with one good zap,
> not to mention having all your intrinsics removed.  You know you find the 
> game easy only because you spent untold hours on this game.  But for 
> beginners (which you once were), this game is no piece of cake.

First of all, contrary to popular belief, wands of cancellation do not
eliminate intrinsics.  Also, as of 3.1.x, they do not remove names from
weapons (if you zap Mjollnir with a wand of cancellation, it just
becomes uncursed and +0).  I actually find wands of cancellation handy
for removing cursed armor.  Just strip off everything else and dump it,
zap yourself and voila! (french for "you can take off that damn armor
now")

Second, I think it is totally inconsistant to allow monsters to zap
wands of death and not cancellation.  Wands of cancellation would have
to become alot less common, sure, and I think you could make it so that
they have a limited range or a worse chance to hit that other wands (I'm
sure somebody can come up with some transparantly bogus reason for it),
but I think it would certain make the game alot more interesting.  And,
newbie or not, the end of the game is significantly easier than the
beginning, at least, until you kill the Wizard of Yendor and start
getting the random cursed items and the summoned monsters.  The game is
currently unbalanced, and I think that allowing monsters to zap wands of
cancellation would go quite a long way toward rebalancing things.  I
also like the idea of not being able to genocide liches (well, I don't
LIKE the idea, but I think it would make things more balanced).  Few
things in the game are bigger pains in the ass than master liches. 
Titans are already ungenocidable, why not liches?

